DTSTART:20260624T223000Z
DTEND:20260624T233000Z
DTSTAMP:20260624T000000Z
SUMMARY:Community Cat Workshop w/ CPAW NJ
DESCRIPTION:Community cats are not homeless. They just live outside! Join 
 Amanda from Communities Promoting Animal Welfare NJ (CPAWNJ) (and a special 
 fuzzy guest) for an informative program on caring for outdoor cats. Learn 
 best practices for managing community cats\, navigating neighbor concerns\, 
 and understanding the benefits of Trap-Neuter-Return (TNR) for both cats 
 and their caregivers. The session will connect residents with local 
 resources for spay/neuter services and highlight ways to support Glen Ridge 
 cats through volunteering.\n\nAdult Program | Registration Required\nOPEN 
 to all\n\nCommunities Promoting Animal Welfare NJ (CPAW NJ)( is is a 
 501(c)(3) charity dedicated to keeping cats out of shelters by controlling 
 the outdoor cat population. CPAW NJ promotes TNR through trapping\, 
 education and financial assistance for TNR to caretakers in northern New 
 Jersey.
LOCATION:Glen Ridge - Meeting Room\, Glen Ridge Free Public Library
ORGANIZER;CN="Glen Ridge Library":MAILTO:events@glenridgelibrary.org
CATEGORIES:Health & Wellness
UID:LibCal-10286-16816396
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/16816396
END:VEVENT
