BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20260630T230000Z
DTEND:20260701T000000Z
DTSTAMP:20260630T000000Z
SUMMARY:Hidden History: World War I & II Propaganda Posters - VIRTUAL REV250
DESCRIPTION:The iconic Uncle Sam “I Want You” poster is widely 
 recognized\, yet few understand its true wartime significance or that it 
 was part of a broader array of propaganda used during World Wars I and II 
 to influence public sentiment. Zoom in with historian\, Kassidy Cobb\, as 
 she explores various World War I and II propaganda posters and discuss just 
 why these all-too-often ignored pieces of history are vital to our 
 understanding of the past.\n\nVirtual Program | Registration Required\nOpen 
 to all\nCan't make it in person? Register to access the event recording for 
 7 days!
LOCATION:Glen Ridge Free Public Library
ORGANIZER;CN="Glen Ridge Library":MAILTO:events@glenridgelibrary.org
CATEGORIES:Lecture
UID:LibCal-10286-16733450
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/16733450
END:VEVENT
