BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20260709T193000Z
DTEND:20260709T203000Z
DTSTAMP:20260709T000000Z
SUMMARY:Plant-Based Creations w/ Mary Silvestri - Adult Cooking Workshop
DESCRIPTION:\n	\n		\n			\n			Come and join us for a culinary delight.  
 We'll discuss the benefits of gardening.  Create delicious\, all natural\, 
 healthy dips using vegetables from your garden.  These recipes require 5 
 ingredients or less. They're quick and easy to make and enjoy as an 
 appetizer for parties\, holiday spreads\, picnics or just to impress family 
 and friends.  You'll be able to watch how to make 3 different veggie dips\, 
 and receive a copy of the recipes.\n\n			Led by Mary Silvestri\, certified 
 teacher\, entrepreneur\, and host and producer of Culinary Basket\, a local 
 cable cooking show.\n\n			Adult Program | in-person | Registration 
 Required\n			Open to ALL patrons\n\n			About Mary: Mary Silvestri\, MA\, is 
 a multifaceted educator.  She’s traveled around the world and is 
 passionate about cooking\, gardening and being out in nature.  She loves 
 creating new recipes and sharing them with others.  She was the owner of a 
 pesto sauce company she created by growing basil in her own 
 backyard.\n			\n		\n	\n
LOCATION:Glen Ridge - Meeting Room\, Glen Ridge Free Public Library
ORGANIZER;CN="Glen Ridge Library":MAILTO:events@glenridgelibrary.org
CATEGORIES:Health & Wellness
UID:LibCal-10286-17092329
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/17092329
END:VEVENT
