SUMMARY:New Dinosaurs? New Discoveries? Ask a Real Paleontologist!
DESCRIPTION:Unearth the Latest Dinosaur Discoveries with a Real 
 Paleontologist! This summer\, the adventure continues beyond the pages of 
 your favorite books!\n\nAs part of CSLP's Unearth a Story™ summer reading 
 program\, public libraries and their patrons are invited to a FREE virtual 
 event featuring paleontologist Dr. Aki Watanabe on July 15 at 1:30 PM 
 Eastern. A 1\,000-seat Zoom room is available\, so registration will be 
 capped. \n\nHave you ever wondered how scientists uncover the secrets of 
 dinosaurs? Join us for an exciting journey into the world of fossils\, 
 fieldwork\, and groundbreaking discoveries as Dr. Watanabe shares some of 
 the most fascinating dinosaur finds from the past year. You'll 
 discover:\n\n\n	New dinosaur discoveries making headlines around the 
 world\n	How paleontologists search for and study fossils\n	The cutting-edge 
 technology helping scientists unlock ancient mysteries\n	What dinosaur 
 fossils can tell us about evolution\, behavior\, and life millions of years 
 ago\n	Answers to your questions during a live Q&A session\n\n\nDr. Watanabe 
 is an Associate Professor of Anatomy at the New York Institute of 
 Technology and a Research Associate in the Division of Paleontology at the 
 American Museum of Natural History. \n \nDig into discovery. Explore the 
 latest science. Unearth a Story™ with us on July 15! \n\nRegister here:  
 https://www.cslpreads.org/amnh-guide/#webinars
LOCATION:Glen Ridge Free Public Library
ORGANIZER;CN="Glen Ridge Library":MAILTO:events@glenridgelibrary.org
CATEGORIES:Special Event
UID:LibCal-10286-17099507
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/17099507
END:VEVENT
