SUMMARY:Narrative Threads: New Jersey Quilt & Textiles - VIRTUAL
DESCRIPTION:For centuries\, people in New Jersey have been producing a 
 stunning variety of textiles. Zoom in with a representative from the Museum 
 of Early Trades & Crafts (METC) as they explore historic pieces from the 
 museum's collection\; including quilts\, woven textiles\, lace pieces\, and 
 the tools involved in making textiles.\n\nVirtual Program | Registration 
 Required\nOPEN to all
LOCATION:Glen Ridge Free Public Library
ORGANIZER;CN="Glen Ridge Library":MAILTO:events@glenridgelibrary.org
CATEGORIES:Lecture
